=== 1) protocole MCP sans authentification ===
  initialize                                    HTTP 401  WWW-Auth: Bearer scope="programs:read profile:read reports:read report {"error":"unauthorized"}
  tools/list                                    HTTP 401  WWW-Auth: Bearer scope="programs:read profile:read reports:read report {"error":"unauthorized"}
  prompts/list                                  HTTP 401  WWW-Auth: Bearer scope="programs:read profile:read reports:read report {"error":"unauthorized"}
  resources/list                                HTTP 401  WWW-Auth: Bearer scope="programs:read profile:read reports:read report {"error":"unauthorized"}
  resources/templates/list                      HTTP 401  WWW-Auth: Bearer scope="programs:read profile:read reports:read report {"error":"unauthorized"}
  tools/call (search_programs)                  HTTP 401  WWW-Auth: Bearer scope="programs:read profile:read reports:read report {"error":"unauthorized"}

=== 2) forger un jeton avec la bonne audience (aud=MCP) ===
  initialize + jeton forge (aud=MCP, sig invalide)HTTP 401  WWW-Auth: Bearer error="invalid_token", error_description="token faile {"error":"invalid_token","error_description":"token failed validation"}
  tools/list + jeton forge                      HTTP 401  WWW-Auth: Bearer error="invalid_token", error_description="token faile {"error":"invalid_token","error_description":"token failed validation"}

=== 3) enforcement de l audience : un jeton API (aud=API) est-il accepte par le MCP ? ===
  tools/list + jeton forge aud=API              HTTP 401  WWW-Auth: Bearer error="invalid_token", error_description="token faile {"error":"invalid_token","error_description":"token failed validation"}

